# Photoshop Backend — API & Service Conventions

## API Routes
- Use Zod for runtime input validation on ALL route handlers — parse before any business logic
- All endpoints must return structured error responses: `{ error: { code, message, details? } }`
- All async route handlers must have explicit try/catch — no unhandled promise rejections
- Use custom error classes that extend a base AppError with an HTTP status code
- Route files define routes only — business logic belongs in services/

## Services
- Service functions must be pure where possible — accept inputs, return outputs, no side effects on globals
- Image processing functions must validate input dimensions and format before operating
- Long-running operations (batch processing, large image transforms) must support cancellation
- Always clean up temporary files in a finally block, even on error paths

## Data Validation
- Never trust client-supplied Content-Type — verify MIME type from file bytes
- Validate all numeric parameters have sane bounds (e.g., filter intensity 0–100)
- Use Zod .transform() for coercion, not manual parsing

## Logging
- Use structured JSON logging with requestId correlation
- Log at INFO for request start/complete, WARN for recoverable errors, ERROR for failures
- Never log image binary data or user file contents
